{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"451ae9891f6725f72cbd8f16340ce3314b25a347b5fb167318ee573b46400f37","digest":{"component_or_area":"MCP writes adapter","key_entities":["src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py::unlink_tickets","rebar.unlink","relation","src/rebar/_commands/unlink.py::unlink_cli","src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py::unlink","docs/mcp-reference.md","scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py","tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_unlink_relation.py","FastMCP","id1","id2"],"problem_keywords":["MCP","unlink_tickets","relation selector","parameter parity","write-surface","optional parameter","delegate forwarding"],"propositions":["MCP unlink_tickets lacks an optional relation parameter that is already supported by the public library and CLI, preventing callers from selecting which edge to remove when a ticket pair holds multiple relations","The registered FastMCP callable signature and schema both omit the relation parameter, making it impossible to express the selector in MCP requests","The unlink_tickets delegate call forwards only id1 and id2 to rebar.unlink, losing the relation value even if the parameter were added to the signature","Omitting relation should preserve the documented pair-scoped fallback of removing the most-recent edge","Signed parity requirement on restoring-shallow-blobfish mandates zero intended divergences across library, CLI, and MCP write surfaces"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787369802621483001,"uuid":"73116616-be23-4010-9a13-b3df4e3aff9d"}